  // The employer took it down; nothing to do and nothing to worry about.
  posting_gone: { kind: "closed", waitingOn: "nobody" },
  // A captcha or an anti-bot wall. The coding agent takes this down, not them.
  wall: { kind: "pending", waitingOn: "us" },
  // Ours by definition.
  our_bug: { kind: "pending", waitingOn: "us" },
  // Nobody could classify it, so nobody can be asked to act on it.
  unknown: { kind: "pending", waitingOn: "us" },
};
```

And the `it.each` test: `expect(userFacingFailure(outcome)).toEqual(EXPECTED[outcome]);`

Also add a test that verifies waitingOn follows kind (the invariant). This is a nice addition to the new shape:

```ts
it("always agrees with its own kind", () => {
  for (const outcome of FAILURE_OUTCOMES) {
    const p = userFacingFailure(outcome);
    if (p.kind === "actionable") expect(p.waitingOn).toBe("candidate");
    else if (p.kind === "closed") expect(p.waitingOn).toBe("nobody");
    else expect(p.waitingOn).toBe("us");
